{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "fac71914-3eb0-4d52-8364-4781a45abc45",
    "name": "mock-api",
    "description": "## mock-api\n\nThis collection provides a mock API layer for simulating a complete user authentication and account management backend. It is organized into three functional groups:\n\n### Auth\n\nHandles all authentication flows, including user **registration**, **login**, and **token re-authentication** (`re-auth`). Use these endpoints to simulate onboarding new users and managing session tokens.\n\n### User\n\nCovers core user account operations such as **logout**, **password updates**, **account deletion**, **session management**, **listing users**, and retrieving **user info**. These endpoints represent the full lifecycle of a user account.\n\n### Profile\n\nContains the **create-profile** endpoint for setting up a user's profile after registration.\n\n---\n\nThis collection is intended for use with a mock server to enable frontend development and integration testing without requiring a live backend. Global variables `BASE_URL` and `accessToken` are used across requests for base URL configuration and bearer token authorization.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "40773121"
  },
